      "statusChangeID": "62d3172d591e9c44bae57176",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "in progress",
      "value": "Technically, this will be improved in a later update that we're working on so I will mark this as in progress. However, I should mention that you should never rely on every serialization to happen exactly once or even for every serialization to happen at all. It is not a messaging system, it is a syncing system. You may receive the same data twice or you might not receive some intermediate values at all. What matters is that everyone is \"eventually consistent\" and lands on the same value after the dust settles.\nYou are welcome to add your own logic on top of this to create a messaging system, such as a timestamp to ignore repeated messages or an array of values to queue up and send multiple quick messages at once.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
